            <ArticleTitle>Intracoronary Doppler flow to monitor the results of selective saphenous vein graft thrombolytic therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Selective intracoronary thrombolytic therapy has recently been advocated as a technique to recanalize occluded coronary bypass grafts. We report a novel approach for monitoring the results of this treatment utilizing a coronary artery doppler flow guidewire. This approach may optimize the duration of thrombolytic treatment in these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
